>Is decnet just for vax/vms or are other computers connected?
>Is it a nationwide, world wide, etc?
>Are there gateways to other networks?
>Is decnet new/old and does it have any historical significances?

There is a common misunderstooding. DECNET isn't a Network in the
same sense as BITNET or INTERNET. It's the protocol you can use
on most DEC-Computers. 

There are some real networks using DECNET as a protocol, besides
the local networks.

The two large networks i know of, are  SPAN and HEPNET.
Both are interconnected, so they are in real one network.
HEPNET = High Energy Physics Network
I don't know the spelling of SPAN, but it's the network of
the astrophysics, (it's sponsored/maintained by the NASA).

SPAN/HEPNET is worldwide and has gateways to Internet and Bitnet.

