This may not be the proper group to post this request, but for the 
groups I can see on my system it seemed the best.

I am looking for a way to do wide-area-network disk volume shadowing.
The two approaches that immediately come to mind are:

1)  A software product to perform the disk shadowing.  If one is a available:

    a)  Does it support more than two disks in a volume set?
    b)  Is it compatible with Dec's HSC shadowing?

2)  A hardware product.  In particular, a black box that can set between
