> The problem here is how to get these files onto a MicroVAX disk in UNIX
> format.  To do that, you're going to need to run one of the programs

? I have a Ultrix Micro Vax , and access to a bulk of VMS VAXes. The way 
I transfer the stuff is to read the tar file under VMS using 

$ mount/for/recsize=10240/blocksize=10240/nohdr3 tapedevice
$ copy tapedevice: filename 

and voila, there is one huge file on VMS which is a tar file. This, then, 
is copied to UNIX either by writing it on a TK50 on a VMS Micro VAX file 
using the same hack, or by using DECNET, or UCX. If you have neither of these
possibilities, try to use KERMIT or such a program. The file is readable 
under UNIX tar, as 

% tar -tf filename 

will give you a listing. :-) maybe it takes 
a while. Alos, it might be that I misunderstood the problem. 

Cheers, 
