A windfall of DEC hardware and software is coming upon my 
organization and I won't be able, for many reasons, to run UNIX
on it.  As a result, I need to get feedback from people using them
now about the applications I am being offered to see if they will fill
our Office Automation needs.

The basic hardware will be a MicroVAX 3100 with 32 MB of RAM and
768K of HD, and a total of 12 Asynch lines feeding VT320's and
VT330's.

Aside from an accounting package to be named later, we are being
offered:

WPS-Plus Word Processing
DECalc-Plus Spread Sheet
CDD/Plus and VAX Rally 4GL
Scriptprinter (apparently a Postscript software driver for the LN03)

In general, I'd appreciate reports of the pros and cons of this
stuff from folks who are using it, and recommendations of
preferred substitutes and why.

I also have general questions about this.  As I am rather insulated 
from the decision makers at this stage, I'd like some information 
from Net folks so I'm somewhat armed when I do get to talk with them, 
as I'll be responsible for administering this beast.

About half our terminals will be text and half will be
graphics.  This suggests that there is some WYSIWYG in WPS-Plus.
Else, why bother with the VT330's?

How much is there?  Sufficient for minimal page layout (like
newsletters)?  Perhaps on the order of Word Perfect 5.0?

I see no email on this list.  Is something like that built-in to
VMS, as it is in UNIX?  Will it serve to mail documents,
spreadsheets, etc. around to users as in an integrated manner, or
would I really need something like All-In-One to do that?

In other words, with this package, will I end up sheparding
files around to users within a workgroup, because the software
won't let them do it themselves (one of my greatest fears...)?

Also, what options are available to me for hooking this beast up
to the Net and gatewaying VMS mail to UUCP?

All email comments appreciated. 

