products often is that the DecNet is a layered products, i.e. the 'open' 
in the programs is replaced by 'netopen' etc. This means that the UNIX 
world still cannot access the files from applications as if they were local 
UNIX files. Does anyone know more about 3rd party products on UNIX 
which directly access files (i.e., mods of the kernel)? 

On the other hand, VMS is also accessible by Unix. This includes UCX, 
and Wollongong, CMU-TEK and others. Looking at the rest of the world, 
the DEC hardward is o.k., but not necessarily determining applications 
across boundaries. Things might change with OSI but currently I'd like 
it better if I have a reasonable TCP/IP implementation on DEC (i.e., 
