In article <2926@teda.UUCP>, bob@teda.UUCP (Bob Armstrong) writes...
>  We have a relatively old C compiler, version 2.4, so this may be a problem
>that has been fixed.
> 

If the problem is in the CRTL, then it will not be fixed by upgrading the
compiler.  The CRTL is maintained by the C developers, but it is shipped with
VMS, not C.  The solution, if the problem is in the CRTL is to upgrade and see
what that will do or not use a search list.  Another option is to get into the
RMS data structures and release the channels yourself.

scott


